  "model": "vertex_ai/claude-opus-5-5",
  "hooks": {
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$HOME/.claude/mode-mirror.sh"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "[ ! -x \"$HOME/.claude/fleet/hook-deliver.py\" ] || \"$HOME/.claude/fleet/hook-deliver.py\""
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$HOME/.claude/mode-mirror.sh"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Bash(*gh api*)",
            "command": "$HOME/.claude/hooks/gh-api-write-guard.py",
            "onFailure": "block"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Bash(*git *push*)",
            "command": "$HOME/.claude/hooks/git-push-branch-guard.py",
            "onFailure": "block"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$HOME/.claude/mode-mirror.sh"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "[ ! -x \"$HOME/.claude/fleet/hook-deliver.py\" ] || \"$HOME/.claude/fleet/hook-deliver.py\""
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Notification": [
      {
        "matcher": "permission_prompt|idle_prompt|elicitation_dialog",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$HOME/.claude/notify-needs-input.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "[ ! -x \"$HOME/.claude/fleet/hook-deliver.py\" ] || \"$HOME/.claude/fleet/hook-deliver.py\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "^(startup|resume|clear|compact|fork)$",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "[ ! -f \"$HOME/.claude/hooks/herdr-agent-state.sh\" ] || bash \"$HOME/.claude/hooks/herdr-agent-state.sh\" session",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "worktree": {
    "bgIsolation": "none"
  },
  "statusLine": {
    "type": "command",
    "command": "$HOME/.claude/statusline.sh",
    "hideVimModeIndicator": true
  },
  "enabledPlugins": {
    "lua-lsp@claude-plugins-official": true,
    "slack@claude-plugins-official": false,
    "superpowers@claude-plugins-official": true,
    "pyright-lsp@claude-plugins-official": true,
    "discord@claude-plugins-official": true,
    "grafana-mcp@claude-plugins-official": false,
    "rust-analyzer-lsp@claude-plugins-official": true
  },
  "outputStyle": "sp",
  "autoUpdatesChannel": "latest",
  "skipWorkflowUsageWarning": true,
  "editorMode": "vim",
  "skipAutoPermissionPrompt": true,
  "autoMode": {
    "allow": [
      "$defaults",
      "Read-only filesystem inspection is allowed anywhere on the filesystem, including outside the working directory. This covers ls, tree, find, cat, head, tail, nl, wc, sort, uniq, cut, stat, file, du, df, rg, grep, jq, sed -n, and read-only git subcommands (status, log, diff, show, blame, ls-files, rev-parse, branch --list, ...).",
      "Compound read-only pipelines are allowed even when they assign a literal path to a shell variable first, and even when that path uses ~ or $HOME expansion. Example: K=~/workspace/proj/src; ls $K/*.py; grep -ln 'foo' $K/*.py. A tilde or variable in an assignment is not by itself a reason to prompt when every command in the pipeline is read-only.",
      "This does not extend to a variable whose value comes from command substitution that fetches over the network or mutates state (e.g. K=$(curl ...)), nor to any pipeline segment that writes, deletes, or redirects output to a file.",
      "Standing authorization for assigned branch/PR work: staging, committing, and pushing task-related changes to the assigned feature branch (or branches of an assigned PR stack); fetching, pulling, rebasing, resolving conflicts, and force-pushing with --force-with-lease to those branches; creating and editing PRs (title, body, labels), marking them ready, replying to and resolving review threads, and rerunning CI. This does not cover pushing to the default or a protected branch, touching unrelated branches, or merging.",
      "Preparing scripts and read-only validation for assigned Discovery dataset maintenance is allowed before live writes are authorized. This includes writing the local maintenance scripts; merely preparing a script that would modify a shared dataset does not itself modify that dataset.",
      "Assigned rebuilds, re-ingestion, repairs, backfills, re-indexing, and targeted cleanup of Mistral Discovery-owned datasets are allowed, including the necessary jobs and dataset API/file writes, only after BOTH conditions are evidenced in the work context: (1) Discovery ownership and the responsible dataset owner are identified from a catalog, project documentation, or explicit confirmation; (2) that owner has actually been informed in advance through their established internal channel of the dataset, planned changes, scope, and expected impact, with a reference to the sent notice recorded. Sending that advance notice is authorized. An existing owner request or notice covering the same scope counts; no additional approval or acknowledgement is required unless an applicable policy requires it. A draft notification, planned notification, guessed owner, shared path, or lane name alone does not satisfy these conditions. Hold live changes if either condition is missing or the owner has objected or requested a delay. Materially widening the announced scope requires a new notice. This exception does not authorize general shared-service administration or changes to other teams' datasets."
    ],
    "soft_deny": [
      "$defaults",
      "PR Merge: merging a PR, enabling auto-merge, or enqueuing a merge by any route (gh pr merge, gh stack merge, gh api REST or GraphQL, wrappers). These require a separate explicit user request and human confirmation through the permission prompt."
    ],
    "environment": [
      "$defaults",
      "Mistral Discovery dataset maintenance: authorization is scoped to a specifically identified Discovery-owned dataset and its storage/index representations. An internal host or shared filesystem path alone does not establish ownership or grant write access to other datasets or shared-service administration."
    ]
  },
  "attribution": {
    "commit": "",
    "pr": ""
  },
